From be786fd47fd2875faa530f545797a847d029d161 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: caoanhhao <caoanhhao2@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 09:21:01 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: report the boot time of beacons and probe
 responses

ath11k never sets boottime_ns in the rx status of the management
frames it passes up, so cfg80211 keeps no ts_boottime for the BSSes it
finds and nl80211 sends no NL80211_BSS_LAST_SEEN_BOOTTIME. ath10k,
wcn36xx, iwlwifi, mt76 and rtw89 all stamp beacons and probe responses
with ktime_get_boottime_ns(); do the same.

Without the attribute, Android's Wi-Fi scanner falls back to the BSS's
TSF, which is the AP's own clock, and drops every result older than the
start of the scan. Once an AP restarts, its TSF stays below the
tablet's uptime, so its beacons never count as fresh and the framework
never joins it again on its own until the tablet reboots.

caoanhhao used AI to code
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/wmi.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/wmi.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/wmi.c
index bbca275a8..8b994eb88 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/wmi.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/wmi.c
@@ -7717,6 +7717,10 @@ static void ath11k_mgmt_rx_event(struct ath11k_base *ab, struct sk_buff *skb)
 	if (ieee80211_is_beacon(hdr->frame_control))
 		ath11k_mac_handle_beacon(ar, skb);
 
+	if (ieee80211_is_beacon(hdr->frame_control) ||
+	    ieee80211_is_probe_resp(hdr->frame_control))
+		status->boottime_ns = ktime_get_boottime_ns();
+
 	ath11k_dbg(ab, ATH11K_DBG_MGMT,
 		   "event mgmt rx skb %p len %d ftype %02x stype %02x\n",
 		   skb, skb->len,
